[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1119,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 1158,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154351,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1158,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipoma is a benign subcutaneous neoplasm consisting of mature adipocytes intermingled with clusters of small, thin-walled vessels that often contain fibrin thrombi.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1120,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 1159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154352,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8861/0 Angiolipoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1121,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154353,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E80.0Y &amp; XH3C77 Other specified lipoma and Angiolipoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1122,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154354,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1123,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154355,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154356,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas most commonly involve the extremities, with approximately 50% arising in the forearm, followed by the trunk {35668116}. Rare intraosseous angiolipomas have been described {36368613; 37363475}. Intramuscular haemangiomas and the so-called angiolipoma of parenchymal organs or of the CNS are different lesions that have larger vessels and should not be confused with angiolipoma {29614355; 7356383}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154357,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas most frequently present as multiple, small, tender/painful subcutaneous nodules {7026412}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154358,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas are common, representing 5&ndash;17% of all lipomas {25621058}, and affect a wide age range, most commonly from the second to sixth decades of life. There is a male predominance {7026412; 35668116}. An increased familial incidence has been described in approximately 5% of cases, with an autosomal dominant mode of inheritance {17511936}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154359,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154360,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas typically have a normal karyotype with only rare cases showing rearrangement of chromosome&nbsp;13 {9130991; 7515663}. The majority (80%) have low frequency <em>PRKD2</em> variants. PRKD proteins play a role in angiogenesis {28139834}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154361,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas appear as well-circumscribed yellowish to reddish nodules.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154362,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas are composed of mature adipocytes and clusters of branching, capillary-sized vessels embedded in a collagenous stroma. The vessels often contain fibrin thrombi. The vascularity is more prominent at the periphery of the tumour {7026412}. The proportion of adipocytes and vessels is variable, and some lesions are almost completely composed of vascular channels (cellular angiolipoma) {2294783}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154363,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Aspirations show the same findings of lipoma, with tissue fragments of adipocytes containing a single large, clear cytoplasmic vacuole with a compressed rim of cytoplasm and a small nucleus with an inconspicuous nucleolus. In addition, small vessels are increased in number at least focally and show fibrin thrombi, best seen in cell block material {12920746}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154364,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1134,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154365,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> mature adipose tissue; variable clusters of capillaries; often with fibrin thrombi.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1132,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154366,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1133,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154367,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 1172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas are benign and show no tendency for local recurrence.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]